h\"\n\n\ndef load_api_key():","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"609b63721cb4b7403288e783d047bb1072dd6043596c2c13271820e37c4c2001","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/tavily_search.py","start_line":11,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0d4529e3900f47a0a053944a4c02fdfa","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"scripts/tavily_search.py","start_line":63,"end_line":76},"finding":null,"explanation":"The script sends the user-provided query and optional content-related parameters to Tavily's external API, which creates a real data disclosure boundary. In a web-search skill this transmission is expected functionality, but it is still a valid privacy/security issue because there is no explicit consent prompt, redaction step, or warning preventing users from sending sensitive data to a third party.","remediation":"Add an explicit user-facing notice that queries and any requested raw content will be sent to Tavily, and require confirmation before transmitting potentially sensitive input. Implement input classification/redaction for secrets, personal data, and internal-only terms, and consider disabling raw-content retrieval by default unless the user opts in.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/tavily_search.py","start_line":63,"end_line":76}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1795,"completion_tokens":245,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2040},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_outpu